# Target C: face-coupled finite folds, diameter currency and exact blockers

Date: 2026-10-07. Authority: audit.77.
**Proved candidates awaiting independent audit**, with explicit regressions.
No promotion. Full-source isolates remain part of every endpoint.

## 1. Exact finite source equations

Let the actual contact core be a connected plane graph whose bounded
quadrilateral faces are strict unit rhombi. Opposite rhombus edges define
the complete stopped trains. For each oriented contact edge ij put
q_ij=p_j-p_i and choose a sign s_tau in {-1,+1} for its train.
For each bounded nonquadrilateral face, with boundary occurrences, require

`sum_(ij in partial f) s_(tau(ij))*J(q_ij)=0`.                 (1)

Rhombus equations already cancel on opposite edges. Bounded face cycles
span the graph's cycle space, including articulation/bridge cases; thus
(1) permits path-independent integration of a core field U satisfying

`U_j-U_i=s_(tau(ij))*J(q_ij)` on every contact edge.           (2)

This rederives only the needed integration implication of the proof-only
face-closure modules; it does not import their rank or Hall conclusions.
Signs are **coupled by actual face equations**, not independent owners
for crossing multishears. No outer-to-outer train supply is assumed.

Define actual finite coordinates

`X_i(phi)=cos(phi)*p_i+sin(phi)*U_i` on the core.              (3)

Every contact edge has exact unit length, because its vector is
`cos(phi)*q+sin(phi)*s*J(q)`. Equation (1) gives finite closure as well
as infinitesimal closure; no higher-order correction is being omitted.
For each retained isolate choose its U_i explicitly as a free full-source
coordinate, and use (3) for it too. These coordinates satisfy no automatic
contact-core rigidity or lower/upper theorem. Their complete pairs remain
binding. At phi=pi/2 the source endpoint is U, with all old labels retained.

For **every** source pair ij, put r=p_j-p_i and v=U_j-U_i. Its exact
squared distance along (3) is

`cos(phi)^2*|r|^2+sin(phi)^2*|v|^2`
`+2*cos(phi)*sin(phi)*(r dot v)`.                            (4)

This includes actual old diameters, inactive upper exceptions, all core
noncontacts, isolates and crossing-train pairs. All lower and upper bounds
are the same full finite list, 1<=expression<=D^2. At the quarter-turn,
these comparisons are simply 1<=|v|^2<=D^2. Source cardinality is fixed;
a collision is a lower violation, not a silently discarded label.

A continuous feasible path is not required for a finite competitor.
In particular opposite-signed trains at a rhombus exchange its two
unit-rhombus diagonals at the quarter-turn: their squared lengths are
`|a+b|^2` and `|a-b|^2`, swapped. Both exceed one in a strict rhombus.
This exact statement does not claim immunity during a small shear or
from other lower pairs.

## 2. Canonical stress supplies strict diameter currency

Use the canonical relative-interior stress alpha>0 on actual contacts,
beta>0 on actual diameters, sum beta=1. On the contact core write
`Omega=L_C(alpha)-L_H(beta)`.
The canonical C-I selected defect and ZR imply Omega>=0 and
`ker Omega=span{1,p_x,p_y}` on this core only. To make the PSD implication
explicit: on the grounded/zero-sum contact space, the selected condition
`B^-1-Q^T*Lambda^-1*Q>=0` says every singular value of
`Lambda^-1/2*Q*B^1/2` is at most one, hence
`Lambda-Q*B*Q^T>=0`. Positive interior Schur reconstruction gives the
full core Omega>=0. This is the canonical selected-matrix/Schur input,
not a new universal-stress claim about isolated coordinates.

Virial gives sum alpha=D^2. Equation (2) gives

`trace(U^T*Omega*U)=D^2-sum_H beta_h*|U_j-U_i|^2`.            (5)

If U is nonaffine on the core, this trace is strictly positive by the
exact affine kernel. Consequently the weighted old-diameter mean at the
quarter-turn is strictly below D^2. At least one old actual diameter
has shortened. Nonconstant signs alone do not imply nonaffinity: with
only two contact directions a nonconstant sign state can be affine.
With at least three distinct projective contact directions, an affine
contact flex has symmetric part zero and is rotation plus translation;
then every nonconstant sign state is nonaffine. Alternatively check
nonaffinity directly from the realized coordinates.

**Finite endpoint criterion.** If such a nonaffine face-coupled sign
state admits chosen coordinates for all retained isolates and satisfies

- every old contact remains exactly unit (automatic on the core);
- every old noncontact pair is strictly greater than one;
- every old actual diameter pair is at most D;
- every old nondiameter pair is strictly below D;

then the endpoint is impossible in a canonical triangle-free source.
It retains all labels and all old contacts, creates no new contact or
triangle, and creates no new diameter pair. Equation (5) removes at
least one old actual diameter pair. Either diameter is strictly smaller,
or it equals D with fewer actual diameter pairs at unchanged contacts.
Both violate the canonical lexicographic endpoint.

Thus the weighted stress resolves the endpoint currency **once full
feasibility is supplied**. It does not assert that a mean decrease bounds
each diameter, or infer feasibility from (1).

## 3. A source-realized sign compatibility graph

Take two distinct unit edges ij and jk. Their other endpoints are a
noncontact in a triangle-free old graph. Let L=|p_k-p_i|. If their signs
are opposite, the quarter-turn identity is

`|U_k-U_i|^2=4-L^2`.                                      (6)

For L>sqrt(3) this is below one. For L=sqrt(3) it is exactly one,
creating a unit triangle with the two preserved edges through j.
Therefore a triangle-free quarter-turn endpoint must use the **same**
sign on these two trains whenever L>=sqrt(3).

Form Gamma on actual train variables by inserting precisely these
source-realized two-hop relations. Signs are constant on its connected
components. Contract Gamma before solving (1); enumerate coupled signs
on the resulting components and check (4). If Gamma is connected, only
the two global quarter-turn rotations survive, so this entire nontrivial
quarter-fold mechanism is blocked in that source. This is a scope closure
for the mechanism, not C-II closure.

Some exact geometric consequences help identify Gamma:

- At a degree-five triangle-free unit vertex, all cyclic neighbour gaps
  are strictly greater than pi/3. Every nonconsecutive neighbour pair
  has angular separation greater than 2pi/3. The complement of a 5-cycle
  is connected, so all five incident trains have the same sign.
- At a degree-four vertex, opposite neighbours in cyclic order have
  separation greater than 2pi/3; each opposite incident pair has the
  same sign. The two pairs need not have the same sign as each other.
- Along consecutive collinear unit edges, L=2 and opposite signs collide.
- Around a convex unit face, a boundary turn at most pi/3 gives L>=sqrt(3)
  and couples its two consecutive signs. If all turns are at most pi/3,
  every boundary sign is the same. The prescribed strictly curved six-wall
  family has this property for sufficiently small curvature: side turns
  are small and corner turns are below pi/3.

These are constraints on actual realized edges. They are not inferred
from a path forest, owner topology, planarity alone or infinitesimal
crossing independence. Rhombus diagonals have L<sqrt(3), so (6) correctly
does not invent an extra blocker at their quarter-turn endpoint.

## 3.1 Complete convex-face transition classification

There is a stronger exact restriction on any convex unit face, including
a nonquadrilateral terminal host. In a fully lower-feasible, triangle-free
quarter-fold, a sign transition at a face vertex is possible only when
its exterior turn is **strictly greater** than pi/3; at equality the new
three vertices are a unit triangle. Convex total turn is 2pi, so at most
five vertices are eligible. A cyclic sign pattern has an even number of
transitions. Two transitions would select one contiguous plus arc whose
vector sum is the difference of two distinct source endpoints, hence
nonzero; this contradicts its part of (1). Therefore a nonconstant pattern
has exactly four transitions.

Let their cyclic source vertices be a,b,c,d, choosing the two plus arcs
from a to b and c to d. Face closure gives

`(p_b-p_a)+(p_d-p_c)=0`, hence `p_a+p_c=p_b+p_d`.

Thus the **four actual transition vertices form an inscribed parallelogram**,
and all four have exterior turns greater than pi/3. At the quarter-turn
its two diagonals are exchanged in length. This is an exact necessary
classification, not a generic-position assertion. In particular any
convex face with fewer than four eligible corners, or with no such actual
inscribed parallelogram among its eligible vertices, forces all its
boundary train signs equal. Add these face relations after Gamma before
enumerating the remaining coupled system. A unit rhombus satisfies the
four-corner alternative; the regular or curved six-wall does not.

A complete rectangular eight-vertex unit wall provides the sharp simple
example: four right-angle transition corners do form a parallelogram,
and its opposite-side sign patterns give the two reflections plus two
rotations, all full-source feasible and all affine. No blanket prohibition
on convex faces or on four transitions is inferred.

## 4. Exact regressions against incomplete finite ledgers

### A. Weighted contraction and old upper feasibility do not suffice

Use the regular unit hexagon p_k=exp(i*k*pi/3), contact cycle C6 and
three opposite diameter pairs H, D=2. Set alpha=2/3 on each contact and
beta=1/3 on each diameter. Its signed Omega is PSD with affine kernel
and rank three. Indeed the integer matrix A=3Omega satisfies A^2=6A,
so x^T*A*x=|A*x|^2/6>=0, and has trace 18 and rank three.

Enumerate all 64 signs on its singleton trains and require (1). There
are ten face-coupled states, two constant and eight nonconstant. Every
nonconstant state strictly lowers the weighted old-diameter mean and
satisfies every old actual diameter upper inequality at the quarter-turn.
Nevertheless each has a collision among source vertices. Hence no such
state is a feasible source. The exact complete pair checker records the
lower failures; no label is removed on collision.

The hexagon is not globally optimal and is not asserted to satisfy the
canonical mixed-rigidity/C63 conclusions. The six-site center-plus-regular-
pentagon configuration is unit-separated, triangle-free, and has diameter
squared (5+sqrt(5))/2<4, proving nonglobality. The regression tests the
specified stress/finite-mean inference, not a canonical source theorem.

### B. Old diameters can shrink while inactive pairs restore their count

For M=2,3,4 use the full unit rhombic grid
`{i*u+j*v:0<=i,j<=M}`, with u=(1,0), v=(5/13,12/13).
Its contact graph is triangle-free. Its 2M complete rhombus trains have
no exceptional face equations. Gamma connects all u-direction trains,
and separately all v-direction trains. Complete sign enumeration leaves
four quarter-turn states with full lower feasibility, all affine.

Opposite signs on the two families swap the long and short corner
diagonals. The sole old actual diameter strictly shortens, but the old
inactive opposite corner pair becomes a new diameter of the same length.
Contacts, triangle-freeness, cardinality and diameter-pair count are all
unchanged. Thus checking only actual old diameter rows would falsely claim
a currency win. The full endpoint correctly rejects the proposed strict
inactive-upper hypothesis. A separate continuous shear toward a square
beats this rhombic family; it is explicitly nonglobal.

The verifier certifies full pair/contact/diameter ledgers, exact face
closure, Gamma components, stress identities and complete sign universes
for these finite examples. It does not establish universal sign existence,
canonical source geometry or global optimality.

## 5. Exact remaining full-core obligation

For every sufficiently large canonical source in the surviving coupled
train regime, either find a nonaffine sign state satisfying (1), Gamma
and the complete finite endpoint inequalities, or derive enough actual
geometry from their exhaustive blockers to construct a different move.
No binary state is guaranteed. A large real kernel of C_face does not
imply a nonconstant sign vector; constants alone can intersect a high-
dimensional real kernel. Gamma may close this quarter-turn subroute.

Two materially different continuations are: nonbinary finite train angles
satisfying the exact nonlinear face equations
`sum_(ij in partial f) exp(i*theta_tau)*q_ij=0`, and collective deletion/
refill through the actual Delaunay metric-defect skeleton. The macro
container and cap/core-release obligations remain open. The endpoint here
is full-source and finite, but existence is the missing theorem.
